   "text": {
    "L1": "Distances can be compared only when they use the same unit.",
    "L2": "A bigger number is not always a longer distance. The unit matters.",
    "L3": "First, change each distance to metres.",
    "L4": "For example, 2 km 75 m becomes 2,075 m. The other distance, 2,700 m, stays the same.",
    "L5": "Now compare 2,075 m and 2,700 m. So 2,700 m is farther by 625 m.",
    "L6": "To order distances, change them to metres and place them from the smallest to the largest.",
    "L7": "For 1,800 m, 1 km 900 m, and 2 km, the order is 1,800 m, 1 km 900 m, then 2 km.",
    "L8": "Now order these three distances from shortest to longest."
   },
